% ============================================================================
% precipitation-minimum-diameter.query.adj — a worked recall over the
% meteorology precipitation-minimum-diameter library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "how big does a hail
% pellet have to be?": it states no meteorology fact of its own — it only
% `import`s the grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves
% each `?` against the `precipitation_min_diameter` rows and returns the
% threshold + the table's source/locator/trust.
%
% The third query runs the relation BACKWARD (bind the diameter 0.5, recall
% which precipitation type it names — rain). A precipitation type whose
% cited span states no diameter figure (snow) abstains honestly — the
% engine never invents a threshold.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli precipitation-minimum-diameter.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "precipitation-minimum-diameter.adj"

? precipitation_min_diameter(rain, $MinDiameterMm)  % expect 0.5
? precipitation_min_diameter(hail, $MinDiameterMm)  % expect 5
? precipitation_min_diameter($Precip, 0.5)          % reverse bind — expect rain
? precipitation_min_diameter(snow, $MinDiameterMm)  % expect abstain — the cited span gives snow no diameter figure
